    "intro_html":  "Florentine on a menu means there is spinach in it, a naming convention we inherited from French kitchens honoring Catherine de Medici. What it means for your kitchen is that frozen chopped spinach, which costs almost nothing, is about to carry a creamy turkey bake. Each serving lands at 572 calories with \u003cstrong\u003e35 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.30\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). There is a whisper of curry powder in the sauce that sounds strange and tastes exactly right.",
